**1. A method for wireless communication, comprising:**

establishing, by a base station, a radio connection with a user equipment (UE), the radio connection including a wireless link between the UE and a radio transceiver point communicatively coupled to the base station and to a virtual machine executing on a computing platform;

configuring, by the base station, a first functional split of Layer 2 processing for the radio connection such that a first subset of Layer 2 processing functions is performed by the radio transceiver point and a second subset of the Layer 2 processing functions is performed by the virtual machine;

communicating user-plane data for the UE between the radio transceiver point and the virtual machine in accordance with the first functional split;

determining, by the base station based on at least one operating condition associated with the UE, the radio transceiver point, a transport network, or the computing platform, to change the first functional split to a second functional split;

in response to the determining, transferring Layer 2 context associated with the UE between the radio transceiver point and the virtual machine and reassigning at least one Layer 2 processing function from one of the radio transceiver point or the virtual machine to the other of the radio transceiver point or the virtual machine; and

continuing communication of the user-plane data between the UE and the base station according to the second functional split while maintaining the radio connection,

wherein the Layer 2 processing functions comprise at least two of medium-access-control scheduling, hybrid automatic repeat request processing, radio-link-control segmentation or reassembly, retransmission processing, packet-data-convergence processing, header compression, ciphering, integrity protection, or packet reordering.
